Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:45:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 44/71] Stop the compaction prompt from dropping reasoning
 nobody priced

The summarization prompt names no active turn, and undecided reasoning from
the turn that just ended was dropped there as it always had been. But that
prompt is the last one on the prefix the turn left behind, and the request
before it carried the reasoning: leaving it out rewrote the prompt from the
start of the turn and re-prefilled the whole window at full price. With the
memory refresh on, its own pricing pass happened to stamp the reasoning
first and hide this; with it off, every compaction in the measured sessions
was billed at 0% cached (76,991 / 79,944 / 80,466 / 80,054 input tokens).

A prompt naming no turn now keeps reasoning that has an owning turn and no
verdict. When reasoning is not priced at all, the drop is written onto the
item the moment its turn ends, so that prompt leaves out exactly what the
request before it left out instead of putting it back.

